igned for reading and research.","evidence_claim":"The university describes Fenwick's North Study Area as a 600-square-foot, two-story study-research space with open seating for 20 and marks it as not reservable.","source_url":"https://library.gmu.edu/support/fenwick","source_title":"Your Support Can Build A Library for the Future","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Inside Fenwick Library and available during posted building hours. The official space description marks the area as not reservable.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gmu-fenwick-presentation-practice-room","subject_type":"study_space","entity_name":"Fenwick Presentation Practice Room","title":"Rehearse the Presentation, Not Just the Slides","subtitle":"A technology-supported room for teams of up to five","notes":"Reserve this third-floor room for a timed rehearsal, load your visuals in advance, and let every group member practice using the equipment.","short_summary":"A small, technology-equipped room purpose-built for presentation rehearsal.","evidence_claim":"George Mason University describes Fenwick's third-floor Presentation Practice Room as a 150-square-foot technology-supported rehearsal space accommodating five students.","source_url":"https://library.gmu.edu/support/fenwick","source_title":"Your Support Can Build A Library for the Future","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Reservation required. University Libraries limits its study rooms to Mason students, faculty, or staff with a valid Mason NetID.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gmu-johnson-center-study-rooms","subject_type":"study_space","entity_name":"Johnson Center Study Rooms","title":"Book a Johnson Center Study Room","subt